# Lumenhold Academy — 简体中文 (zh-CN) translation of content/events/jobs.grim
# Maintained by `node tools/grim.js i18n zh-CN`. Translate the text after "="; keep {tokens}.
# "# en:" shows the English source. [hash] marks the English version a line was translated from;
# lines marked STALE need updating — after fixing the text, delete the [hash] and re-run the tool.


@event lib_biting_book
# en: The Book That Bites
title [e0be45] = 会咬人的书
# en: Reshelving in the zoology section, a fat leather book clamps onto your finger and refuses to let go. The head librarian, without looking up, says: "Stroke the spine."
text [68fee7] = 你在动物学区上架时，一本厚厚的皮面书咬住了你的手指，死活不松口。图书馆馆长头也不抬地说：“摸摸它的书脊。”
# en: A thick leather book with tiny teeth along its pages snapping at a hand reaching for it on a high shelf.
scene [b648b2] = 一本书页边缘长着细牙的厚皮书，正冲着伸向高处书架的手咬去。
# en: Muzzle it with a belt
opt.left.label [c9d229] = 用皮带把它的嘴捆上
# en: You wrestle it into submission and shelve it. It growls at you every time you pass for the rest of the term.
opt.left.say.1 [91c33d] = 你把它摁服了，放回书架。接下来整个学期，你每次经过它都会冲你低吼。
# en: Stroke the spine and read it
opt.right.label [b279ad] = 摸摸书脊，读一读
# en: It purrs, opens and turns out to be a fascinating treatise on carnivorous plants. It only bites twice more. The reshelving waits until tomorrow.
opt.right.say.1 [ad9f03] = 它发出呼噜声，自己翻开了——原来是一部关于食肉植物的精彩论著。它只又咬了你两次。上架的活只好等到明天。

@event lib_overdue_professor
# en: Overdue
title [40f62b] = 逾期未还
# en: Professor Thorne returns a book that is eleven years overdue. The fine, by library rules, is forty crowns. He looks at you. You look at the ledger.
text [f16fb3] = 索恩教授还了一本逾期十一年的书。按照图书馆规定，罚款是四十克朗。他看着你。你看着罚款簿。
# en: A severe professor towering over a library desk, a stack of books under one arm, a very small student assistant on the other side holding a fines ledger.
scene [9af617] = 一位严厉的教授高高站在图书馆柜台前，胳膊下夹着一摞书，柜台另一边一个小小的学生助理捧着罚款簿。
# en: Waive the fine
opt.left.label [20e10a] = 免了罚款
# en: "Hm," says Thorne. You can't tell if you've earned his respect or lost it.
opt.left.say.1 [30eaf0] = “嗯。”索恩说。你说不清自己是赢得了他的尊重，还是失去了它。
# en: Enforce the rules
opt.right.label [32a605] = 照章办事
# en: A long silence. Then he pays, in exact change. "Good," he says, and you could swear he almost smiles.
opt.right.say.1 [a7c7e3] = 漫长的沉默。然后他付了钱，分文不差。“很好。”他说，你敢发誓他差点笑了。

@event lib_restricted_cart
# en: The Restricted Cart
title [1e31b9] = 禁书推车
# en: You are asked to wheel the Restricted Section returns to the vault. The cart's chain has come loose. One of the books has fallen open on a page that is writing itself.
text [e83ef7] = 你被派去把禁书区归还的书推回书库。推车的锁链松了。其中一本书摊开在一页正在自己书写的纸上。
# en: A wheeled library cart chained shut, piled with black-bound books, parked alone in a candlelit aisle.
scene [e3b4b3] = 一辆用锁链锁着的图书推车，堆满黑皮书，孤零零地停在烛光摇曳的过道里。
# en: Close it without looking
opt.left.label [69f4b5] = 不看，直接合上
# en: The book snaps shut with a sound like a disappointed sigh. The vault door clangs. The head librarian notes the time, approvingly.
opt.left.say.1 [2fb0b1] = 书啪地合上，发出一声像是失望的叹息。书库的门哐当关上了。馆长记下了时间，满意地点点头。
# en: Read a few lines
opt.right.label [40815b] = 读上几行
# en: The words crawl off the page and up your sleeve. That night, you can't get warm.
opt.right.say.1 [166cd2] = 文字从书页上爬出来，钻进了你的袖子。那天夜里，你怎么也暖和不起来。
# en: A spell for walking through mirrors. You will never try it. Probably.
opt.right.say.2 [ee6c9d] = 一个穿过镜子的咒语。你永远不会去试的。大概吧。

@event tavern_brawl
# en: Brawl at the Newt
title [6ed513] = 蝾螈酒馆斗殴
# en: A dwarf and a troll disagree about the price of turnips, and the Gilded Newt erupts. A chair flies past your head. The owner is hiding behind the bar, gesturing at you to do something.
text [f434ad] = 一个矮人和一个巨魔为芜菁的价格吵了起来，镀金蝾螈酒馆瞬间炸了锅。一把椅子从你头顶飞过。老板躲在吧台后面，比划着让你想想办法。
# en: A low-beamed tavern mid-brawl: a chair in mid-air, a dwarf on a table, cider sloshing everywhere.
scene [d9c407] = 一间低梁小酒馆正在混战：一把椅子悬在半空，一个矮人站在桌上，苹果酒洒得到处都是。
# en: Duck behind the bar too
opt.left.label [56a05c] = 也躲到吧台后面
# en: You crouch beside the owner and share a bag of crisps while the room destroys itself.
opt.left.say.1 [87132f] = 你蹲在老板旁边，和他分吃一袋薯片，看着整个屋子自我毁灭。
# en: Break it up
opt.right.label [12966a] = 上去劝架
# en: You slam a tray on the bar and bellow. Silence. The troll apologises. The dwarf tips you fifteen crowns.
opt.right.say.1 [b417fb] = 你把托盘往吧台上一拍，大吼一声。全场安静。巨魔道了歉。矮人给了你十五克朗小费。
# en: You step in. Someone's elbow steps into your face.
opt.right.say.2 [763c5b] = 你上前一步。不知谁的胳膊肘也上前一步，到了你脸上。

@event tavern_star_coin
# en: A Generous Stranger
title [678324] = 慷慨的陌生人
# en: A hooded stranger nurses a cider all evening and leaves a tip: a black coin stamped with a hollow star. "For the student," they say. "Tell Kael Dumont his family sends regards."
text [b2c4b8] = 一个戴兜帽的陌生人一整晚只喝了一杯苹果酒，留下的小费是一枚印着空心星的黑色硬币。“给这个学生的，”对方说，“转告凯尔·杜蒙，他的家人向他问好。”
# en: A hooded figure at a corner table sliding a black coin across the wood, its surface stamped with a dark star.
scene [fe800a] = 角落桌旁一个戴兜帽的身影把一枚黑色硬币推过木桌，币面上印着一颗暗星。
# en: Refuse the coin
opt.left.label [999c57] = 拒绝这枚硬币
# en: The stranger shrugs and pockets it. When you look again, the corner table is empty and the cider is frozen solid.
opt.left.say.1 [53629a] = 陌生人耸耸肩，把它收回口袋。你再看时，角落的桌子空了，那杯苹果酒冻成了冰。
# en: Take it
opt.right.label [18a43f] = 收下它
# en: The coin is cold as ice and heavier than it should be. You find yourself turning it over in your pocket for days.
opt.right.say.1 [2b7ed8] = 硬币冷得像冰，比看上去要重。接下来好几天，你发现自己总在口袋里摩挲它。

@event tavern_extra_shifts
# en: More Shifts
title [bc17d5] = 加班
# en: The owner is short-handed. "Double shifts for a month," he says. "Double pay. I know you've got studies, but you've also got rent."
text [daff5a] = 老板人手不够。“一个月双班，”他说，“双倍工钱。我知道你还要上学，但你也还要交房租。”
# en: A ruddy tavern owner leaning on the bar, wiping a mug, a rota pinned behind him covered in crossed-out names.
scene [205014] = 一个红光满面的酒馆老板靠在吧台上擦杯子，身后钉着的排班表上划掉了一个又一个名字。
# en: Decline
opt.left.label [eaef39] = 拒绝
# en: "Fair enough," he says, and asks again next week.
opt.left.say.1 [2ad5ce] = “行吧。”他说，然后下周又来问。
# en: Take the extra shifts
opt.right.label [124a34] = 接下加班
# en: A month of late nights and early lectures. Your purse is heavy. So are your eyelids.
opt.right.say.1 [bef75a] = 一个月的深夜打工和清早上课。你的钱袋沉甸甸的。眼皮也是。

@event tavern_broken_glass
# en: Broken Glass
title [6a7d8c] = 打碎的酒杯
# en: {A tray of tankards meets a regular's elbow, and the floor is suddenly all glass.|Another tray, another floor of glass. The Newt goes through tankards the way other places go through napkins.|Glass on the floor again, and the same regular's elbow to blame.} {The regular is very sorry, loudly.|Everyone lifts their feet.|The dog is already heading for it.}
text [f64d54] = {一托盘酒杯撞上了一位常客的胳膊肘，地上顿时满是碎玻璃。|又一托盘，又是一地玻璃。蝾螈酒馆消耗酒杯的速度，就像别处消耗餐巾。|地上又是玻璃，又是那位常客的胳膊肘惹的祸。} {那位常客大声地连连道歉。|所有人都把脚抬了起来。|那条狗已经朝碎片走过去了。}
# en: A tavern floor glittering with broken tankards, a server crouching with a cloth, a dog padding closer.
scene [6d91e1] = 酒馆地板上闪着碎酒杯的光，一名侍应蹲着拿抹布，一条狗正慢慢凑近。
# en: Clear it by hand, fast
opt.left.label [b1cbdf] = 徒手快快收拾
# en: {You have it cleared before the dog gets there, with a cut across your palm to show for it. The landlady binds it with a bar towel.|Fast and thorough, apart from the sliver you find in your thumb at midnight.|You beat the dog to it by a whisker and a nicked finger. The landlady gives the dog a sausage for its trouble.}
opt.left.say.1 [7d2b36] = {你赶在狗之前收拾干净了，手掌上多了一道口子作证。老板娘用一条吧台毛巾给你包上。|又快又干净，只是半夜你才在拇指里发现一根玻璃碴。|你以一根胡须的差距和一根划破的手指抢在了狗前面。老板娘给了狗一根香肠作为补偿。}
# en: Fetch the broom and do it properly
opt.right.label [32e157] = 拿扫帚好好扫
# en: {By the time you're back with the broom, three customers have left with their cider unfinished. The landlady counts them.|You sweep slowly and safely while the bar goes dry. The landlady taps the clock.|You go for the broom, and the landlady has to hold the dog back by the collar while the customers' cider goes warm.}
opt.right.say.1 [e43aa3] = {等你拿着扫帚回来，已经有三个客人苹果酒没喝完就走了。老板娘一个个数着。|你慢慢地、稳稳地扫，吧台那边却断了酒。老板娘敲了敲钟。|你去拿扫帚，老板娘只好揪着狗的项圈拦住它，客人们的苹果酒都放温了。}

@event tavern_after_closing
# en: After Closing
title [c895a2] = 打烊之后
# en: {Your shift tonight runs until the Newt closes, long after the last barge.|Another late shift. By closing time the lake will be dark.|Late shift again. You've stopped expecting to see the last barge.} {season == "winter": These nights the shore path is ice under snow.|{Fog comes off the water most nights now.|The shore path has no lamps.|Somebody always sings, badly, on the way home.}} It's a long walk round the lake to the castle.
text [920705] = {你今晚的班要上到蝾螈酒馆打烊，那时末班驳船早就开走了。|又是晚班。到打烊时，湖面会一片漆黑。|又是晚班。你已经不指望赶上末班驳船了。} {season == "winter": 这些夜里，湖岸小路上是雪下的冰。|{这阵子湖上夜夜起雾。|湖岸小路上没有灯。|回家路上总有人在唱歌，唱得很难听。}} 绕湖走回城堡，路还很长。
# en: A lantern-lit shore path at night, a tired server walking alone beside black water, the castle's towers far off.
scene [f876cc] = 夜里一条提灯照亮的湖岸小路，一名疲惫的侍应独自走在黑水边，城堡的塔楼远在天边。
# en: Walk the shore path
opt.left.label [8e64c1] = 走湖岸小路
# en: {Two hours round the lake, and every noise in the reeds is something. You reach the gates with wet boots and a turned ankle.|You walk home in the dark and slip twice. You fall into bed as the first bell rings.|You walk home with the other late workers, singing badly to keep the dark off. You're hoarse by the gates, and late to bed.}
opt.left.say.1 [aebb96] = {绕湖走了两个钟头，芦苇里每一声响都像有什么东西。你走到城门时靴子湿透，脚踝也扭了。|你摸黑走回去，滑倒了两次。第一遍钟响时你才倒在床上。|你和其他上晚班的人一起走回去，唱着难听的歌驱散黑暗。到城门时嗓子哑了，睡得也晚了。}
# en: Sleep by the Newt's fire
opt.right.label [66046e] = 睡在酒馆炉边
# en: {The landlady lends you a blanket and the settle by the fire. You wake at dawn smelling of woodsmoke and miss the first lecture.|You sleep on the settle under somebody's coat and catch the morning barge, too late for your first class.|You hear the others singing their way home along the shore and choose the fire. The settle is lumpy, and you miss the first lecture anyway.}
opt.right.say.1 [cf7c9a] = {老板娘借你一条毯子，让你睡炉边的长椅。你在黎明醒来，一身木烟味，错过了第一节课。|你盖着不知谁的外套睡在长椅上，搭上了早班驳船，却赶不上第一节课了。|你听见别人沿着湖岸唱着歌回去，自己选了炉火。长椅硌得慌，第一节课你照样错过了。}

@event apoth_wrong_label
# en: A Mislabelled Jar
title [2e5055] = 贴错的标签
# en: The jar labelled "Sleeping Draught" is green. Sleeping Draught is blue. You're fairly sure the green stuff is Draught of Unending Hiccups. Old Pell is very proud of his labelling.
text [90816e] = 标着“安眠药剂”的罐子是绿色的。安眠药剂是蓝色的。你很确定这绿色的东西是“无尽打嗝药剂”。老佩尔对自己的标签工作非常自豪。
# en: Shelves of glass jars in a narrow shop, one jar labelled SLEEPING DRAUGHT glowing an ominous green.
scene [da4c60] = 狭窄店铺里一排排玻璃罐，其中一只标着“安眠药剂”的罐子发出不祥的绿光。
# en: Quietly fix the label
opt.left.label [d3ca76] = 悄悄改掉标签
# en: Nobody ever knows. Somewhere, a customer sleeps soundly instead of hiccupping for a week.
opt.left.say.1 [3b7685] = 永远没人知道。某个地方，一位顾客安然入睡，而不是打一星期的嗝。
# en: Point it out to Pell
opt.right.label [4225c6] = 告诉佩尔
# en: Pell goes red, then thanks you gruffly and slips you three crowns "for your eyes".
opt.right.say.1 [cdda86] = 佩尔脸一红，粗声道了谢，塞给你三克朗，“算你眼尖”。

@event apoth_poor_mother
# en: Can't Afford It
title [f4bd61] = 买不起
# en: A woman counts out coppers for fever tonic. She's fifteen crowns short. Her son coughs into her coat. Pell is in the back room.
text [1d93f2] = 一位妇人一枚枚数着铜板买退烧药。还差十五克朗。她的儿子靠在她外套上咳嗽。佩尔在后屋。
# en: A tired woman at a shop counter counting copper coins, a small child coughing beside her.
scene [6ddd5b] = 一位疲惫的妇人在柜台前数着铜币，身边一个小孩在咳嗽。
# en: Charge the full price
opt.left.label [9ea316] = 照价收钱
# en: She leaves without it. The bell on the door rings for a very long time.
opt.left.say.1 [b36f54] = 她没买成就走了。门上的铃铛响了很久很久。
# en: Pay the difference yourself
opt.right.label [28226a] = 自己垫上差价
# en: You slip the tonic into her basket. Next week a pie appears on the counter with your name on it.
opt.right.say.1 [8762e7] = 你把药悄悄放进她的篮子。下周，柜台上出现了一个写着你名字的馅饼。

@event apoth_nightshade_order
# en: The Nightshade Order
title [d8aa3b] = 颠茄订单
# en: A note arrives with a sealed purse: a large order of nightshade, grave-moss and powdered moonstone. Legal, technically. Ingredients for something very old and very forbidden, also technically.
text [7f5f4d] = 一张便条随一只封好的钱袋送来：大量的颠茄、墓苔和月长石粉。严格来说，合法。严格来说，也是某种非常古老、非常禁忌之物的原料。
# en: An order slip on a counter listing a dozen deadly reagents, signed with an elegant, illegible flourish.
scene [fe014b] = 柜台上一张订货单，列着十几种致命试剂，签名是一个优雅却无法辨认的花体字。
# en: Fill the order
opt.left.label [c3e9db] = 照单配货
# en: The courier who collects it never shows his face. The purse is very generous.
opt.left.say.1 [c33bee] = 来取货的信使始终没有露脸。钱袋非常丰厚。
# en: Refuse and report it
opt.right.label [ce8f5b] = 拒绝并上报
# en: The headmistress listens to your report in silence. "Thank you," she says. "Tell no one else." She looks worried.
opt.right.say.1 [5c685a] = 院长沉默地听完你的报告。“谢谢你，”她说，“别再告诉任何人。”她看起来很担忧。

@event stables_hippogriff
# en: Bow to the Hippogriff
title [0d01e9] = 向鹰头马身有翼兽鞠躬
# en: The new hippogriff won't let anyone near the feed trough. The stablemaster says to bow, keep eye contact and not blink. "Whatever you do, don't blink."
text [e114f7] = 新来的鹰头马身有翼兽不让任何人靠近食槽。马厩总管说要鞠躬、保持对视、不许眨眼。“无论如何，别眨眼。”
# en: A proud hippogriff in a straw-strewn stall, head lowered, regarding a stable hand who is bowing very deeply.
scene [3828d0] = 铺满稻草的马厩里，一头高傲的鹰头马身有翼兽低着头，打量着一个深深鞠躬的马厩工。
# en: Leave the feed and run
opt.left.label [4fb2e9] = 扔下饲料就跑
# en: You toss the feed bucket and flee. The hippogriff eats it, and the bucket.
opt.left.say.1 [e88a40] = 你扔下饲料桶就逃。它把饲料吃了，连桶一起。
# en: Bow and hold its gaze
opt.right.label [d95cb6] = 鞠躬，与它对视
# en: It bows back. After that it follows you around the stables like a large, feathered dog.
opt.right.say.1 [9dbab4] = 它回了一个礼。从那以后，它在马厩里跟着你转，像一只长了羽毛的大狗。
# en: You blinked. It knocks you flat against the trough, and you spend the evening in the infirmary with your arm in a sling.
opt.right.say.2 [a82f7a] = 你眨眼了。它一下把你撞倒在食槽边，你吊着胳膊在医务室里度过了整个晚上。

@event stables_dragon_egg
# en: An Egg in the Hay
title [b1a78f] = 草堆里的蛋
# en: Mucking out the far stall, you find an egg the size of a melon, nestled in the hay and steaming gently. It's very warm. It's very definitely not a chicken's.
text [067bf4] = 清扫最里面的隔间时，你在草堆里发现一枚西瓜大的蛋，正轻轻冒着热气。它很烫。它绝对不是鸡蛋。
# en: A speckled egg the size of a melon nestled in hay, steam rising from it, a stable hand's lantern held over it.
scene [bb4b8b] = 一枚西瓜大小、带斑点的蛋窝在干草里冒着热气，马厩工的提灯举在它上方。
# en: Report it to Professor Brask
opt.left.label [983969] = 报告布拉斯克教授
# en: Brask nearly faints. "Smugglers! A firedrake egg!" It's taken to the menagerie. You get a commendation.
opt.left.say.1 [95ded5] = 布拉斯克差点晕过去。“走私犯！火龙蛋！”蛋被送进了动物园。你得到了一份嘉奖。
# en: Keep it
opt.right.label [87c2f5] = 留下它
# en: You smuggle it back to your dormitory wrapped in a scarf. It purrs. Eggs shouldn't purr.
opt.right.say.1 [8852b1] = 你用围巾把它裹好，偷偷带回了宿舍。它在打呼噜。蛋不该会打呼噜的。

@event egg_hatches
# en: It Hatches
title [8c317e] = 破壳了
# en: At 3am your pillow catches fire. The egg has hatched: a firedrake the size of a kitten, delighted with itself and setting fire to everything it loves. It loves you very much.
text [c42d90] = 凌晨三点，你的枕头着火了。蛋孵出来了：一条小猫大的火龙，对自己满意极了，见到喜欢的东西就点着。它非常非常喜欢你。
# en: A tiny red dragon perched on a scorched dormitory pillow, a puff of smoke rising from its nostrils, a horrified roommate in the doorway.
scene [41e73c] = 一条小红龙蹲在烧焦的宿舍枕头上，鼻孔冒出一缕烟，门口的室友吓呆了。
# en: Hand it over to the menagerie
opt.left.label [141f8c] = 交给动物园
# en: Brask takes it gently. "You'll be able to visit." You do, every week. It always tries to set you on fire, affectionately.
opt.left.say.1 [695354] = 布拉斯克轻轻接过它。“你可以来探望。”你每周都去。它总是试图把你点着，满怀爱意地。
# en: Hide it as long as you can
opt.right.label [7752e9] = 能藏多久藏多久
# en: You keep it secret for a month — buying fireproof sheets, raw meat, an asbestos sock — before releasing it in the mountains. It circles once, roaring.
opt.right.say.1 [40bff7] = 你把它藏了一个月——买防火床单、生肉、一只石棉袜子——然后在山里放了它。它盘旋一圈，长啸一声。
# en: The smoke alarm charm goes off in three towers at once. Discovered, singed, and in very deep trouble.
opt.right.say.2 [25dba6] = 三座塔的烟雾警报咒同时响起。被发现了，被烧焦了，而且麻烦大了。

@event stables_night_shift
# en: The Sick Pegasus
title [651cda] = 生病的天马
# en: The oldest pegasus in the stables is sick. Someone has to sit with her overnight, keep her warm, and make sure she drinks. It's unpaid. Old Maud says she'll do it if no one else will. Maud is eighty.
text [e3c4b6] = 马厩里最老的天马病了。得有人整夜守着她、给她保暖、确保她喝水。没有报酬。老莫德说没人去的话她就去。莫德八十岁了。
# en: A white pegasus lying in a moonlit stall, wings folded, a student sitting beside it with a lantern and a blanket.
scene [e7765d] = 一匹白色天马收着翅膀卧在月光照亮的马厩里，一个学生提着灯、抱着毯子坐在它身旁。
# en: Let Maud do it
opt.left.label [e408cf] = 让莫德去
# en: You sleep well. Maud is a little slower the next day.
opt.left.say.1 [d77695] = 你睡得很好。第二天，莫德的动作慢了一些。
# en: Take the night shift
opt.right.label [ead26b] = 你来值夜班
# en: She drinks. You talk to her all night about home. At dawn she stands, shakes her wings, and nuzzles your hair.
opt.right.say.1 [e093f9] = 她喝了水。你整夜跟她聊家乡。黎明时，她站起来抖了抖翅膀，用鼻子蹭了蹭你的头发。

@event tutor_hopeless
# en: The Hopeless Case
title [323c15] = 没救的学生
# en: Your tutee has been trying to levitate a feather for three weeks. The feather has not moved. The tutee is starting to cry. You have one more session before their exam.
text [04a494] = 你辅导的学生已经尝试让一根羽毛悬浮三个星期了。羽毛一动没动。学生快哭了。考试前你们只剩一次课。
# en: A tiny first-year in oversized robes pointing a wand at a feather, which is stubbornly not moving, while a tutor watches with infinite patience.
scene [29897d] = 一个穿着过大长袍的小个子一年级生用魔杖指着一根纹丝不动的羽毛，辅导员以无限的耐心在旁边看着。
# en: Drill the basics, again
opt.left.label [652518] = 再练一遍基础
# en: Wrist, word, will. Wrist, word, will. On the exam, the feather twitches. It's enough to pass. Your own levitation has never been cleaner.
opt.left.say.1 [1d2c6c] = 手腕、咒语、意志。手腕、咒语、意志。考试时，羽毛抽动了一下。够及格了。你自己的悬浮咒从没这么干净过。
# en: Try something unorthodox
opt.right.label [b16c64] = 试点不寻常的办法
# en: You tell them to imagine the feather is in love with the ceiling. It shoots upward and sticks there. They pass with distinction.
opt.right.say.1 [e57332] = 你让对方想象羽毛爱上了天花板。羽毛嗖地升上去，粘在了那里。对方以优异成绩通过。
# en: You tell them to imagine the feather is in love with the ceiling. They are confused. So is the feather.
opt.right.say.2 [79cec2] = 你让对方想象羽毛爱上了天花板。对方很困惑。羽毛也很困惑。

@event tutor_bribe
# en: An Indecent Proposal
title [e847fe] = 不体面的提议
# en: A rich second-year doesn't want tutoring. He wants an essay. "Thirty crowns," he says, dropping a purse on the table. "Nobody needs to know."
text [5e864c] = 一个富家二年级生不想要辅导。他想要一篇论文。“三十克朗，”他说着把钱袋扔在桌上，“没人需要知道。”
# en: A rich student in tailored robes sliding a heavy coin purse across a study table, smiling smugly.
scene [188c2e] = 一个穿着定制长袍的富家学生把一只沉甸甸的钱袋推过书桌，得意地笑着。
# en: Refuse
opt.left.label [cada35] = 拒绝
# en: He sneers and goes elsewhere. You spend the evening on your own essays. Later you see him in detention, scrubbing a cauldron.
opt.left.say.1 [1faaba] = 他冷笑一声，另寻他人去了。你把晚上花在了自己的论文上。后来你看见他在禁闭室里刷坩埚。
# en: Write the essay
opt.right.label [b2934c] = 替他写
# en: His professor recognises your style. You both end up in detention. He doesn't speak to you. Fine.
opt.right.say.1 [955908] = 他的教授认出了你的文风。你们俩都被关了禁闭。他不再理你。正好。
# en: He gets a decent mark. You get thirty crowns and a slightly sour feeling.
opt.right.say.2 [b854de] = 他拿到了不错的分数。你拿到了三十克朗，和一丝酸溜溜的感觉。

@event tutor_prodigy
# en: Surpassed
title [679359] = 青出于蓝
# en: Your newest tutee, a first-year barely a month in, casts in a week what took you a year. Then she asks you a question you can't answer.
text [04f3f6] = 你新带的学生，一个入学才一个月的一年级生，一周就学会了你花一年才学会的咒语。然后她问了你一个你答不上来的问题。
# en: A small first-year casting a dazzling spell that fills a classroom with light, their tutor watching with complicated feelings.
scene [9e6498] = 一个小个子一年级生施展出一道耀眼的咒语，满屋光芒，辅导员在一旁神情复杂。
# en: Bluff an answer
opt.left.label [86ba79] = 硬编一个答案
# en: She nods politely. You both know.
opt.left.say.1 [7e3422] = 她礼貌地点点头。你们俩心里都明白。
# en: Admit you don't know and find out together
opt.right.label [b4d010] = 承认不知道，一起去查
# en: You spend an evening in the library together. She thanks you as if you've taught her something. Maybe you have.
opt.right.say.1 [92c9bb] = 你们在图书馆待了一晚上。她向你道谢，好像你教了她什么。也许你真的教了。

@event courier_storm
# en: Delivery in a Storm
title [d6be36] = 风暴中送件
# en: An urgent parcel needs to cross the lake tonight. There's a storm. The dispatcher offers double pay to whoever's fool enough. Everyone looks at you.
text [7b10ad] = 一件急件今晚必须送过湖。外面有风暴。调度员给愿意去的傻瓜开双倍工钱。所有人都看着你。
# en: A courier on a broom bent low against a lightning-lit sky, a parcel strapped to their back, rain sheeting sideways.
scene [eccc6d] = 一名信使伏低身子骑着飞帚冲进闪电照亮的夜空，背上绑着包裹，雨水横扫。
# en: Wait for the storm to pass
opt.left.label [fd0d0f] = 等风暴过去
# en: The parcel arrives late. The client deducts it from your wages. Rude, but survivable.
opt.left.say.1 [c849f6] = 包裹迟到了。客户从你的工钱里扣了钱。无礼，但还活得下去。
# en: Fly through it
opt.right.label [d49b80] = 穿过风暴
# en: You thread the lightning like a needle and land soaked, laughing, with the parcel dry.
opt.right.say.1 [419505] = 你像穿针一样穿过闪电，浑身湿透地落地，大笑着，包裹却是干的。
# en: Lightning strikes close enough to stand your hair on end. You lose the broom, the parcel and the pay, and gain a limp.
opt.right.say.2 [71c971] = 一道闪电劈得太近，你的头发都竖了起来。你丢了飞帚、包裹和报酬，得了一条瘸腿。

@event courier_whispering_parcel
# en: The Whispering Parcel
title [00dbb7] = 会低语的包裹
# en: Your parcel is addressed to "K. Dumont, Stillwater House". It is ice cold and it whispers when you aren't looking at it.
text [a7f392] = 你的包裹寄给“静水院，K. 杜蒙”。它冷得像冰，你不看它的时候，它会低语。
# en: A brown paper parcel tied with black string on a courier's satchel, frost forming on its corners, faint whispers rising from it.
scene [cef7c7] = 信使挎包上一个用黑绳捆着的牛皮纸包裹，边角结着霜，隐隐传出低语声。
# en: Deliver it unopened
opt.left.label [edbe83] = 原封不动地送达
# en: Kael takes it without a word. His hands shake. The next day, he looks like he hasn't slept.
opt.left.say.1 [6ad92e] = 凯尔一言不发地接过包裹。他的手在抖。第二天，他看起来像一夜没睡。
# en: Peek inside
opt.right.label [95f6de] = 偷看一眼
# en: Inside: a letter in a cold, beautiful hand. "The Star wakes. Come home, or open the door. Your family." You reseal it perfectly.
opt.right.say.1 [49350a] = 里面是一封信，字迹冰冷而优美：“星辰苏醒了。回家，或者打开那扇门。——你的家人。”你把它完美地重新封好。
# en: The seal hisses as it breaks. Kael is waiting at the door when you arrive. He saw. He says nothing, which is worse.
opt.right.say.2 [1d94cc] = 封印裂开时发出嘶嘶声。你到的时候，凯尔已经等在门口了。他看见了。他什么也没说，这更糟。

@event courier_sky_pirates
# en: Sky Pirates
title [933c94] = 空中海盗
# en: Three figures on patched brooms drop out of a cloud and box you in. "Toll," says their leader, a woman with a parrot that is also on a tiny broom. "Eight crowns or the parcel."
text [0892d1] = 三个骑着补丁飞帚的身影从云里冲出来围住了你。“过路费，”领头的女人说，她的鹦鹉也骑着一把小飞帚，“八克朗，或者包裹。”
# en: Three ragged figures on patched brooms surrounding a courier above the clouds, cutlasses glinting.
scene [5f6143] = 云层之上，三个衣衫褴褛、骑着补丁飞帚的身影围住一名信使，弯刀闪闪发亮。
# en: Pay the toll
opt.left.label [a1a28f] = 交过路费
# en: They let you pass with a salute. The parrot salutes too.
opt.left.say.1 [de94eb] = 他们敬了个礼放你过去。鹦鹉也敬了个礼。
# en: Outfly them
opt.right.label [a811f6] = 甩掉他们
# en: You dive through a cloudbank and lose them over the lake. The client tips extra for the excitement.
opt.right.say.1 [b17031] = 你俯冲穿过云堤，在湖面上空甩掉了他们。客户因为这份刺激多给了小费。
# en: They catch you, take the toll, the parcel and your hat. The parrot wears it.
opt.right.say.2 [8905f7] = 他们追上了你，拿走了过路费、包裹，还有你的帽子。鹦鹉戴上了它。

@event broom_courier_bad_landing
# en: A Bad Landing
title [cc3b0c] = 摔了一跤
# en: {The courtyard flagstones are wet, and your broom has opinions about wet flagstones.|Another wet landing. Your knees remember the last one.|Wet flagstones again. You've learned to dread this courtyard.} {You come in too fast.|A gust takes the tail as you drop.|A pigeon chooses this moment to exist.} You hit the ground rolling, and your ankle says no.
text [afa176] = {庭院的石板是湿的，而你的扫帚对湿石板很有意见。|又是一次湿漉漉的降落。你的膝盖还记得上一次。|又是湿石板。你已经学会害怕这个庭院了。} {你降得太快了。|你往下落时一阵风掀起了扫帚尾。|一只鸽子偏偏挑这个时候出现。} 你滚着落了地，脚踝说：不行。
# en: A courier sprawled on wet flagstones beside a broom, parcels scattered across a rain-slick courtyard.
scene [20fcd9] = 一名信使摔倒在湿漉漉的石板上，扫帚在旁，包裹散落在雨水打湿的庭院里。
# en: Finish the round anyway
opt.left.label [bde896] = 坚持送完这一趟
# en: {You limp the last three parcels to their doors. The dispatcher notes your time and, later, your ankle.|You finish the round on one good leg and a great deal of stubbornness. The bruise is spectacular by evening.|You finish the round with a limp and a grudge against pigeons. The dispatcher writes down both.}
opt.left.say.1 [7abcb4] = {你一瘸一拐地把最后三个包裹送到门口。派件员记下了你的用时，后来又记下了你的脚踝。|你靠一条好腿和满满的倔劲送完了这一趟。到晚上，那块淤青壮观极了。|你一瘸一拐地送完了这一趟，还记恨上了鸽子。派件员把两样都记下了。}
# en: Hand your sack to another courier
opt.right.label [54b1a8] = 把邮袋交给别人
# en: {Another courier takes your sack with a sympathetic wince. Half a shift's pay, and an evening with your foot up.|You sit on the loft steps with a cold cloth on your ankle while someone else flies your round. They keep half the pay.|You hand over your sack and spend the evening on the loft steps, foot up, glaring at pigeons.}
opt.right.say.1 [0a316e] = {另一位信使同情地皱了皱眉，接过你的邮袋。半个班次的工钱，外加一晚上把脚架高。|你坐在阁楼台阶上，用凉布敷着脚踝，别人替你飞完了这一趟。工钱他们分走一半。|你交出邮袋，一晚上坐在阁楼台阶上，脚架得高高的，狠狠瞪着鸽子。}

@event broom_courier_lost_parcel
# en: One Parcel Short
title [bffcca] = 少了一个包裹
# en: {Somewhere between the loft and the lecture tower, a parcel has left your sack.|One parcel short, again. You've started counting at every landing.|Another parcel gone. You count at every landing, and still you lose one.} {It was marked "Fragile".|It was marked "Urgent", in red, twice.|It was addressed to a professor.}
text [4d5e5e] = {从阁楼到讲堂塔之间的某处，一个包裹离开了你的邮袋。|又少了一个包裹。你已经开始每次落地都数一遍了。|又丢了一个包裹。你每次落地都数，可还是丢了一个。} {上面写着“易碎”。|上面用红笔写着“加急”，写了两遍。|收件人是一位教授。}
# en: A courier on a windy tower top turning an empty mail sack inside out, the lake far below.
scene [6920d2] = 一名信使站在大风的塔顶上，把空邮袋翻了个底朝天，湖面远在下方。
# en: Retrace your route
opt.left.label [0a2eb5] = 沿原路找回去
# en: {You find it in a hedge behind the greenhouses, whole and slightly damp. You deliver it late, with a story nobody believes.|It's on the boathouse roof. You climb up for it and deliver it with moss on your knees.|You find it in a gutter of the lecture tower and deliver it to the professor, who signs for it without looking up.}
opt.left.say.1 [e91e55] = {你在温室后面的树篱里找到了它，完好无损，只是有点潮。你迟到着送达，还附上一个没人相信的故事。|它在船屋屋顶上。你爬上去拿，送到时膝盖上沾满了青苔。|你在讲堂塔的排水沟里找到了它，送到那位教授手里，教授头也没抬就签收了。}
# en: {You search until dark. The loft takes the parcel's worth from your pay, and the dispatcher stops calling you reliable.|Nothing. The client complains twice, in writing, and the loss comes out of your wages.|The professor's parcel never turns up. The professor does, at the loft, and the loss comes out of your wages.}
opt.left.say.2 [770b4a] = {你一直找到天黑。阁楼从你的工钱里扣了包裹的钱，派件员也不再说你靠得住了。|什么也没找到。客户写信投诉了两次，损失从你的工钱里扣。|教授的包裹始终没找到。教授本人倒是找到阁楼来了，损失从你的工钱里扣。}
# en: Report it lost at once
opt.right.label [5e3d08] = 立刻报告丢失
# en: {The dispatcher writes it in the ledger and the loss in your pay. "Happens," they say, in a voice that means it shouldn't.|You own up straight away. The loft takes it out of your wages, but the dispatcher seems to think better of you for it.|You report it at once. The dispatcher winces at the address, a professor's. It comes out of your pay, with an apology to write.}
opt.right.say.1 [ead196] = {派件员把它记进账本，把损失记进你的工钱。“常有的事，”派件员说，语气却分明是说不该有。|你马上就承认了。阁楼从你的工钱里扣了钱，但派件员似乎对你更看得起了。|你立刻报了丢失。派件员看到地址是位教授，皱了皱眉。钱从你的工钱里扣，你还得写一封道歉信。}

@event job_off_shift
# en: Not Your Shift
title [4d3d09] = 不是你的班
# en: You turn up for work out of habit. The roster by the door says your shifts this term are done, and whoever runs the place says so too. "Nobody pays you to be here today. Go and have a life."
text [d6e252] = 你出于习惯来上工。门边的值班表写着你这学期的班都上完了，管事的人也这么说：“今天没人付钱让你待在这儿。去过你自己的日子吧。”
# en: A duty roster pinned by a staff door, every one of a student's shifts for the term already ticked off.
scene [dbf031] = 员工门边钉着一张值班表，一个学生这学期的每一班都已打了勾。
# en: Take the time for yourself
opt.left.label [52cbbe] = 把时间留给自己
# en: {~You leave before anyone can change their mind, and spend the hours on nothing in particular. It's wonderful.|You take the advice. The place gets on without you, and so, it turns out, do you.}
opt.left.say.1 [78a31c] = {~你趁别人改主意之前就走了，把这几个钟头花在无所事事上。美极了。|你听了劝。这地方没有你照样转，而你，原来没有它也照样过得好。}
# en: Stay and help anyway
opt.right.label [0f8ed9] = 还是留下帮忙
# en: {~You stay, unpaid. Someone notices. Nobody thanks you, and you're tired the next morning.|You lend a hand for an hour. It's not a shift and it doesn't pay, but people remember who stayed.}
opt.right.say.1 [990370] = {~你留了下来，没有工钱。有人注意到了。没人道谢，第二天早上你很累。|你搭了一个钟头的手。这不算一班，也没有钱，但大家记得谁留下了。}
